ndidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Weaknesses: attitude, leadership.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate C has strong reliability, decision making, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation. However creates positive atmosphere suggests good cooperation despite egocentric? Might be contradictory.\n\nCandidate B has stress handling and conscientiousness but uncooperative and grumpy.\n\nCandidate A has anticipation and leadership but unorganized and poor at criticism.\n\nCandidate D has problem solving and responsibility but arrogant and weak leadership.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Probably Candidate C: reliability, decision quality, crew positive atmosphere outweigh communication difficulty? But communication is important for cockpit. Egocentric could be risk.\n\nCandidate B: stress handling is crucial for long-distance, but uncooperative is serious.\n\nCandidate A: anticipation is valuable, but unorganized could affect reliability.\n\nCandidate D: problem solving and responsibility good, but arrogance and weak leadership problematic.\n\nThus maybe Candidate C is best overall, despite communication issues, but positive crew atmosphere suggests cooperation. I'd vote Candidate C.\n\nNow we need to reference existing discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the facts we have, I propose...\"\n\nWe must not dump many facts, just 1-2. Provide evidence: 100% reliability, correct decisions quickly, positive crew atmosphere. Also note communication difficulty as concern but weigh.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: state recommendation for Candidate C, explain why.\n\nMETADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
